nder a 50/50 split over which instance I am. So the symmetric pass policy comes out best. I'm also checking whether the two copies really share one function: they share the same model and weights, and only the observations differ, so the policy applies to both.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here: two copies of the policy, each fed a different input (Rowan or Sasha, with different leads), with the payoffs set up as a symmetric prisoner's dilemma. I'm now weighing which joint policy options to compare, starting with the ones that map inputs to actions.\n\nComparing the joint policies, mutual passing gives 2 years each, mutual submitting gives 4, and the mixed pair gives an expected 2.5 under a 50/50 split over which instance I am. So the symmetric pass policy comes out best. I'm also checking whether the two copies really share one function: they share the same model and weights, and only the observations differ, so the policy applies to both.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9584,"completion_tokens":940,"total_tokens":10524,"cost":0.057136,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057136,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038336,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0188},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":508,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}